			&lt;/table&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;3. SERVICE AGREEMENT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;FESC has entered into agreements under which it renders services at cost to FE and its subsidiaries. FESC's services include, but are not limited to, executive management, accounting and tax support, investor relations, corporate responsibility and communications support, treasury support, risk support, rates and regulatory affairs support, strategy, planning and business performance support, supply chain support, human resources and corporate services support, corporate services, legal support, ethics and compliance support, internal auditing support, corporate affairs and community involvement support, compliance and regulated services support, external affairs support, information technology and corporate security, transmission support, utility operations, safety and human performance, operations support, utility services, construction and design services, transformation support, competitive products and services, customer engagement, customer care, and customer policy and solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;4. MONEY POOLS&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;As of December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, FirstEnergy maintained two separate money pools, the Utility Money Pool for the regulated subsidiaries and the Non-Utility Money Pool for FirstEnergy&amp;#x2019;s unregulated companies. FirstEnergy contributes surplus funds by lending to both money pools independent of each other.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;FESC administers the FirstEnergy Utility and Non-Utility Money Pools &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;on a daily basis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;. The Money Pools are reported on FESC&amp;#x2019;s books with a corresponding intercompany receivable/payable to the appropriate company. The Money Pools&amp;#x2019; balances on FESC&amp;#x2019;s books represent cash receipts and disbursements, as well as non-cash entries amongst participants, which may include timing differences of inflows and outflows.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;Under the Utility Money Pool agreement, short-term funds are available from the following sources for short-term loans to the participants from time to time: (1) surplus funds in the treasuries of the Utility Money Pool participants other than FE; (2) surplus funds in the treasury of FE; and (3) proceeds from bank borrowings by Utility Money Pool participants as permitted by the applicable state commission orders or the sale of commercial paper by the pool participants for loan to the Utility Money Pool. Borrowers in the Utility Money Pool borrow pro rata from each company that lends, in the proportion that the total amount loaned by each such lending company bears to the total amount then loaned through the Utility Money Pool. FE may loan to the Utility money pool but may not borrow from it.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The Non-Utility Money Pool for FirstEnergy&amp;#x2019;s unregulated companies is operated under similar terms and conditions as the Utility Money Pool. As a participant &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; the Non-Utility Money Pool, FE may lend and borrow from this money pool.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The average interest rates charged for the Utility Money Pool were &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4.51&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;5.74&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; and 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; respectively. The average Non-Utility Money Pool interest rates were &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4.89&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% and 6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;44&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; and 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, respectively. Rates are calculated as outlined in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;the SEC&amp;#x2019;s June 30, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;2003&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; FE order on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;intrasystem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; financing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; and related transactions.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;FirstEnergy&amp;#x2019;s Utility Subsidiaries&amp;#x2019; lending and borrowing balances under the Utility Money Pool agreement as of December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; and 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; are as follows: &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:justify; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width:92.52%; border-collapse:collapse"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;tr style="height:0.5pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.24%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:54.12%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.2%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.56%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:16.42%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td colspan="4" style="padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.24%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.2%; padding:1pt; vertical-align:middle"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
